The table presents PK parameters (e.g., AUC, K10, K12) with corresponding units and summary statistics (Mean <math id="S5.F1.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> SD).
Such tables often include complex multi-row headers and embedded textual notes.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F1.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07796v1/Picture2.png" id="S5.F1.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:207/304;" width="207" height="304" alt="Refer to caption">
